triage: fix_game: In the failing scenario the trump was Spades and the defender held 94 (9 of Spades, a trump) against an attack of 61 (6 of Clubs), yet the game offered the defender only ['TAKE']. That is a legal beat under the rules, so the tests' expected discard (defender left with 2 cards) is correct, and the game never builds the defence options. The penalty failures follow from this same bug, because a defender who can never defend keeps picking up cards.
step C: building the game file
triage: fix_game: The rules have only one random event, the S1 shuffle at the start of each deal, and the platform supports seeded deck handling. Different logs from the same seed mean the game file brings in its own non-determinism: an unseeded draw, a clock, or iteration over an unordered collection.
