triage: fix_game: The R10 and R11 failures show the game offering the attacker throw-in cards it may not play. In R10 it offered card 20 (the 8 of Hearts), whose rank matches nothing on the table. In R11 it offered card 18 after the defender had beaten the attack with their last card, when the rules forbid any throw-in. These are implementation errors in the throw-in step, not problems with the rules.
step C: building the game file
step D: evaluating
triage: fix_game: The throw-in options are wrong in the game file. In R10 the table holds 9 (6 of Diamonds) and 1 (7 of Clubs), so only rank-6 and rank-7 cards may be thrown in, but the game offered 20, the 8 of Hearts. In R11 the game offered a throw-in after the defender had beaten the attack with its last card, which rule Step 7 forbids.
