step D: evaluating
triage: fix_tests: In the first two failures the game's throw-in offer was correct: the final offer was [PASS, 9, 18, 27] after attack 0. The tests flagged 1 and 14 because their not_offered checks also caught the attack prompt, where the attacker may legally play any card in hand. The third failure looks like a scenario set-up error and does not show a game bug.
rewriting the independent tests
step D: evaluating
triage: revise_rules: The game was built and behaves as specified, but the design has six choice steps per round where the limit is four. A thoughtless 'always pick the last option' policy also wins about two thirds of its games for either seat. Always beating when possible, with the highest card, is close to dominant, so the decisions carry little real strategy.

